  "notes": "The widest harmonic range on this axis, and that is the point of the entry: the research says Latto works in **both** modes — real I–vi–IV–V motion on the sample-flip pop singles and minor pentatonic on the street cuts. So `session.keys` carries major spellings alongside trap's minor set, `session.scales` weights `major` level with `natural_minor`, and `progressionFamilies` holds genuine major families next to the minor ones. No other entry in this batch does that. The hooks are sing-along-shaped rather than chanted, which is why `melody.structure` is `question_answer` with an arch-leaning contour and a real density band rather than a two-note ostinato. ⚠ `confidence` medium (research: high-medium). The INFERRED parameters are the drum figures — the interviews document the sample-flip construction and the crossover form, not the kick's `syncopation` 0.5 or the hats' `fillDensity` 0.6. ⚠ The verse–pre-chorus–chorus structure is authored as a real alternative rather than a note, with its own `sectionBars` and `sectionRules`, because the research says the pop cuts adopt that form outright. ⚠ The research says 32nd hat rolls under hooks; the roll vocabulary here is `16T` because that is this author's fill band, and the gesture — a fast burst into bar 4 — is the same either way. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
